<title>POLAND: Polish broad money rises 0.5 pct in May 1-20- NBP.</title>
<headline>Polish broad money rises 0.5 pct in May 1-20- NBP.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's broad money rose by 746 million zlotys, or 0.5 percent, in the May 1-20 period to 145.54 billion after a 2.3 percent rise in April, preliminary central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>Broad money supply grew 7.2 percent in the January-May 20 period.  </p>
<p> BROAD POLISH MONEY		    MAY 1-20    APRIL   MAY 1996</p>
<p>  month/month change (pct)		0.5	 2.3	 1.6</p>
<p>  Money in bln zlotys		   145.54    144.80    115.27</p>
<p>  Foreign currency (in bln PLN)	25.33     25.36     21.47</p>
<p>  National currency		     120.21    119.44     93.80</p>
<p>  Cash in circulation		    25.38     25.86     21.83</p>
<p>  Lending to non-financial sector    91.08     90.29     61.82</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
